A choice gives each variant its own constructor. Use `::` to select one. In this example, `Opened` carries no fields and `Resized` takes arguments.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    WindowEvent = {
        Opened,
        Resized | width I32, height I32 = 720 |,
    }

    opened = WindowEvent::Opened
    wide = WindowEvent::Resized(1280)
    tall = WindowEvent::Resized(width = 1280, height = 1080)
]

`wide` uses the default height of 720. `tall` supplies both dimensions.
Match a `WindowEvent` to read its payload.
